
  [1mThe fork:[0m [38;5;153mindex.html[39m loads [38;5;153mapp.js[39m as a classic script — there's no module system in the browser side of this repo. So
  "settings module" has to mean one of three concrete things, and they differ in how the page gets loaded and how you'd
  run the app locally.

  - [1mClassic script, namespaced global[0m — [38;5;153msettings.js[39m next to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, loaded by a second [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag before it, exposing
    something like [38;5;153mwindow.AppSettings[39m. Matches exactly how the app already works; [38;5;153mindex.html[39m still opens straight from
    disk with a double-click. Costs: one more global, and the fix is a load-order dependency in the HTML rather than an
    explicit import.
  - [1mES modules[0m — [38;5;153m<script type="module">[39m, real [38;5;153mexport[39m/[38;5;153mimport[39m between [38;5;153msettings.js[39m and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. A genuine module boundary
    and the modern default. Costs: [38;5;153mtype="module"[39m is blocked by CORS on [38;5;153mfile://[39m, so opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m directly stops
    working — you'd need to serve the directory over HTTP from then on. That's the expensive-to-reverse part.
  - [1mDual-mode module in [38;5;153msrc/[0m — [38;5;153msrc/settings.js[39m that does [38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m for Node and attaches a global for the browser,
    unifying the two halves of the repo. Costs: environment-sniffing boilerplate for a benefit nothing currently needs —
    no Node code reads the API endpoint.

  Cheap to change later: adding environments, renaming the global. Expensive to change later: the ES-module switch,
  because it changes how everyone opens and serves the app.

  [1mMy recommendation: classic script with a namespaced global.[0m Your [38;5;153mCLAUDE.md[39m says match the existing project style
  before introducing new patterns, and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m is already a globals-based classic script. A three-file app doesn't earn
  the cost of breaking [38;5;153mfile://[39m loading to get an [38;5;153mimport[39m keyword — and if you add a bundler later, converting a
  self-contained [38;5;153msettings.js[39m to ESM is a five-line change.
